*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/

*/**/sample-*-run
/*/sample-*-run
sample-*-run

# Local/demo data and credentials for any sample-NNN example directory.
# New examples (sample-002, etc.) get this coverage automatically; add a
# dedicated block above only if an example needs something beyond this.
sample-*/**/*
sample-*/*
sample-*/
sample-*/.env.local
sample-*/**/.env.local
sample-*/**/compose.override.yaml
sample-*/**/compose.override.yml
sample-*/**/data/
sample-*/**/objects/
sample-*/**/tmp/
sample-*/**/.cache/
sample-*/**/*.log
sample-*/**/coverage/
sample-*/**/dist/
sample-*/**/node_modules/
sample-*/**/*.tsbuildinfo
sample-*/**/test-results/
sample-*/**/playwright-report/
sample-*/**/*.db
sample-*/**/*.tfstate*
sample-*/**/generated-credentials/
sample-*/services/build/
sample-*/services/coverage.out
sample-*/services/dependencies.json
sample-*/deploy/helm-rendered.yaml
sample-*/evidence/
evidence/

# Local knowledge-store configuration and data are operator-controlled.
.agents/knowledge-store/config.json
.agents/knowledge-store/data/

# Same for the sibling context store. Its entries are agent-written working
# material with no steward gate in front of them, so a committed database
# would publish unreviewed content -- the failure mode its TTL design exists
# to prevent. roster/context-store/.gitignore covers only the in-repo
# roster/context-store/data/, not a project-local store rooted here.
.agents/context-store/config.json
.agents/context-store/data/

# Local Claude Code settings (not portable across contributors).
.claude/settings.local.json

# Codex CLI marketplace install state, written into whichever checkout the
# install was run against. It pins the revision that happened to be on that
# contributor's disk, so it is stale the moment it is written.
.codex-marketplace-install.json

# Node/TypeScript build artifacts. The only Node code here is the three Cline
# plugins under cline-plugins/ (a single npm workspace); this blanket rule also
# stops a stray local install under a sample-*/ tree being committed.
node_modules/

# Build artifacts for the root-level `cadre` pip/pipx distribution
# (pyproject.toml / cadre_cli/); `python -m build` writes here.
/dist/
/build/

# Agent-created git worktrees (see roster/shared/workspace-isolation.md).
# `.worktrees/` is this repository's own in-root worktree convention;
# `.claude/worktrees/` is Claude Code's own worktree-isolation feature
# writing directly into the project tree. Neither was ignored before this
# entry, which is a latent defect on its own: `cadre select`'s git-status
# mode folds untracked paths into `inputs.changed_files`, so a populated,
# untracked, in-repo worktree would get swept into selection input and
# re-route the whole dispatch decision around its own scratch content.
/.worktrees/
/.claude/worktrees/

# The generated half of plugin/ IS committed, deliberately.
#
# A GitHub-sourced marketplace serves whatever is in the repository tree, so
# an uncommitted distribution means `/plugin marketplace add deagy/cadre`
# installs a plugin with no roles or skills in it. Generated content
# therefore has to be present.
#
# This is not a return to the pre-merge arrangement. What was wrong there was
# *cross-repo* drift: a separate repository pinning a cadre revision in
# cadre-ref.txt, reconciled by a weekly drift-check.yml and a
# regenerate.yml that opened PRs after the fact. Here the source
# (roster/, .agents/skills/, provider/) and its output sit in one commit, and
# validate.yml regenerates and fails on any diff in the same CI run --
# drift cannot outlive a pull request. Never hand-edit generated files under
# plugin/; edit the source and run `cadre generate-plugin --output plugin`.

# The LangGraph engine's uv environment.
/engine/.venv/
cline-plugins/node_modules/

# Go CLI build output (ADR-001-CLI-GO-REFACTOR.md). Never bin/ -- that
# directory is the existing, committed Python dispatcher.
/dist/
